From: Pamela Williard and Mark Pickens <autarch@well.sf.ca.us>
Subject: PPL's and copyrights

> But who does the putative owner of the copyright sue when anonymous
> distribution has been used? Does he sue each person who downloaded
> the material? Am I, the innocent downloader, somehow held
> responsible for finding out if each and every thing I download is
> covered by some copyright, somewhere?
 
> Tim May
 
Absolutely.  This will require extensive monitoring of your personal
life--wups!  Sorry, wrong list.
 
We can expect private copyright agencies to further their own ends by
setting copyright identification standards and exchanging information, so
finding out if you've downloaded something that's covered should become
relatively easy. 
 
However, I don't have a glib refutation of your point that technology will
make copyrights essentially unenforceable.  (Hey, I'm just the idea man.
It's not my job to find a workable enforcement mechanism, but I do hope
someone does.)
 
